#
# Append these lines to /etc/apparmor.d/local/usr.sbin.clamd (Debian's clamd
# profile includes that file), then reload clamd's profile:
#   apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/usr.sbin.clamd
#
# They let clamd run `VirusEvent /usr/bin/clamfleet-agent event`: clamd starts
# /bin/sh (dash on Debian 13; AppArmor sees the resolved path), which inherits
# clamd's profile, and the shell's exec of the agent moves into the dedicated profile
# clamfleet-agent-event (deploy/apparmor/clamfleet-agent-event). Nothing else in clamd's
# profile changes, and nothing else may be executed.

/usr/bin/dash mrix,
/usr/bin/clamfleet-agent Px -> clamfleet-agent-event,
